WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:05.680
High-profile actors are known for making inflated
salaries, but not every coveted role comes

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.030
with a hefty paycheck.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:11.259
We've pulled together a few of the most iconic
roles in the last 30 years that earned actors

00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:14.499
next to nothing—at least by Hollywood standards.

00:00:14.499 --> 00:00:16.460
Barkhad Abdi in Captain Phillips

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:22.830
A 2014 profile in the New Yorker revealed
that Barkhad Abdi made just $65,000 for his

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.580
role as a Somali pirate in the 2013 blockbuster
drama Captain Phillips.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.830
While that may seem like a pretty decent sum
of cash to regular Joes, it's really nothing

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.309
when you consider the movie cost $55 million
to make, and who knows how much of that went

00:00:36.309 --> 00:00:37.870
to star Tom Hanks.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.760
Fortunately for Abdi, the risk seems to have
paid off.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.390
Not only did he win a BAFTA for his critically
acclaimed performance, he went on to earn

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:47.220
Oscar and Golden Globe nominations, as well.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.720
"Look at me."

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.539
"Sure."

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:50.539
"Look at me."

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.120
"Sure."

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.120
"I'm the captain now."

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.429
Jonah Hill in The Wolf of Wall Street

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:58.840
With a directing career that includes iconic
movies like Taxi Driver and Raging Bull, it's

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.159
no wonder actors are willing to do most anything
to be cast in a Martin Scorsese picture.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:08.280
Included on that list: Jonah Hill, who agreed
to the Screen Actor Guild's minimum wage of

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.890
$60,000 to shoot 2013's The Wolf of Wall Street
over seven months.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:18.110
Sure, $60,000 is nothing compared to the $25
million salary that star Leonardo DiCaprio

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.420
made for the same movie.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:23.340
But considering Hill got a surprise Oscar
nomination for his insane performance in a

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.090
Martin Scorsese movie, he probably couldn't
care less.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.220
Brad Pitt in Thelma &amp; Louise

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:34.490
Brad Pitt's star-is-born performance as Geena
Davis' roadside lover in 1991's Thelma &amp; Louise

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:38.870
may have put him on the road to success, but
the role reportedly came with a less-than-sexy

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:39.890
paycheck.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:45.120
Multiple sources have reported that the then-twenty-something
hunk earned a measly $6,000 for his performance.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:49.360
Of course, almost 10 years later, Pitt was
already making upwards of $17 million per

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:54.310
movie and hit the $20 million mark by 2005's
Mr. &amp; Mrs. Smith.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.180
Hilary Swank in Boys Don't Cry

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:01.280
The heartbreaking 1999 bio-pic Boys Don't
Cry, about a woman choosing to live as a man,

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.840
cost a reported $2 million to make, almost
none of which went to its star, Hilary Swank.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.429
The actress herself has admitted this in numerous
interviews, adding her salary was so low,

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:12.780
she couldn't even qualify for health insurance.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.310
Fortunately, her dire financial situation
soon took a turn for the much, much better.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:22.069
After winning a Best Actress Oscar, Swank
made a reported $3 million for her follow-up

00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:24.780
movie, 2001's The Affair of the Necklace.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.230
Bill Murray in Rushmore

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:31.010
In the 2013 book, The Wes Anderson Collection,
writer Matt Zoller Seitz revealed that Bill

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:35.390
Murray earned roughly $9,000 for his performance
in 1998's Rushmore.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:39.830
Plus, when the film's studio, Disney-owned
Touchstone Pictures, refused to pay for a

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:44.920
helicopter for the movie, Murray personally
wrote Anderson a check for $25,000 to cover

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.080
the cost.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.330
Anderson reportedly never even cashed it.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.990
Oprah Winfrey in The Color Purple

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:55.250
Today, legendary talk show host, mogul, and
actress Oprah Winfrey's net worth is estimated

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:00.200
at around $3 billion, but even Oprah had to
start from the bottom and work her way up.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.750
According to music icon Quincy Jones, who
co-produced Winfrey's debut film, 1985's The

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:10.260
Color Purple, Winfrey earned a measly $35,000
for her work on Steven Spielberg's epic.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:15.810
The film ultimately took in almost $200 million
worldwide off a $14 million budget.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.520
Ryan Gosling in Half Nelson

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.420
The budget for 2006 indie drama Half Nelson
was so tight that star Ryan Gosling had to

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:27.530
agree to shoot the movie for $1,000 a week—way
less than some of the high-profile films he'd

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.370
previously made in Hollywood.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:34.810
But like most of the stars on our list, Gosling's
low salary ultimately yielded high returns,

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.730
including an Oscar nomination for his critically
acclaimed performance.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:42.290
He reportedly made a cool $1 million-plus
for his follow-up movie, Fracture, and is

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:45.290
one of the most sought-after actors in the
business today.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.940
Tom Cruise in Magnolia

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:51.410
By the time Paul Thomas Anderson's Magnolia
came around, superstar Tom Cruise could afford

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:53.069
to take a pay cut here and there.

00:03:53.069 --> 00:03:56.890
Still, it's pretty remarkable to just how
low his salary actually dropped.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:02.270
According to multiple reports, Cruise made
just $100,000 for Anderson's drama, next to

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:06.800
nothing compared to the jaw-dropping $20 million
he made that same year for Stanley Kubrick's

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.560
final film, Eyes Wide Shut …

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.780
"I will not apologize for what I want!"

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:13.780
Thanks for watching!

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.120
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

